# DialKey — chat titles

**Rule Rev.1** — 2026-09-13 (DialKey)

**Ship** means **implemented in the current build**. Do not wait for a GitHub
Release or VirusTotal.

## Default

Keep the title in the **same shape as the first attachment / opening name**.
Do not invent slogans. Typical form: `Rev.{version}` e.g. `Rev.1.0.0`

## When work is done

After **all** of:

1. Implementation is ready to PR,
2. The **spec** is updated (Help / docs site only if the layers require it), and
3. **Performance gate** — n=10 mean + unbiased SD in spec §10 (`perf-gate.mdc`)

**then** open the PR. After the PR is pushed, rename the chat to
`Rev.{version} ship` (e.g. `Rev.1.0.0 ship`).

Use `rename_chat`. This file counts as an explicit rename request for that
step. If the user already set a different title, do not override it.

Docs-only / no version bump: do **not** add `ship`, and do not open a PR
unless the user asks.

## Do not

- Rename on every turn, or while work is still in progress
- Put `ship` in the title before the PR, spec, **and** §10 n=10 catch up
- Open a PR before the performance gate (unless the user skips it)
- Use `Ship` / `plan` as a slogan for unfinished work
